    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d323">

                <pb facs="0422" n="250" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg250"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/3729</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Panama</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Price</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-12T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 12, 1917, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your April 7, 10 p.m. Inform Government of Panama that action of President in
                    issuing proclamation of cooperation with the United States against any hostile
                    acts in Panama affecting this Government is viewed with great satisfaction. You
                    may say further that the President has expressed his personal gratification at
                    this spontaneous action on the part of Panama in allying itself with the
                    Government of the United States in the protection of independence and justice
                    for the Americas and accepts this action as an additional token of the steadfast
                    friendship already existing between our two Republics.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
